<title>DENMARK: Deutsche Telekom boosts Tele Danmark.</title>
<headline>Deutsche Telekom boosts Tele Danmark.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish telecom group Tele Danmark rose three percent on Monday, borne on the slipstream of demand for shares in Germany's Deutsche Telekom.</p>
<p>The share closed up nine crowns at 301 crowns on the Copenhagen exchange. It is also traded in New York.</p>
<p>Analysts said that prices set for the partial privatisation of Deutsche Telekom were likely to lift other companies in the industry.</p>
<p>&quot;If the indicative prices are achieved, then most other European telecom shares are undervalued,&quot; a dealer said.</p>
<p>--Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969650</p>
